WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.214
Let’s say you’re trying to
find some solid information

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.740
about a serious health
problem that concerns you,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.400
like high blood pressure,
or diabetes.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.040
Yet, everywhere you look,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.760
someone’s trying to sell you
something like vitamins,

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.000
yoga mats, blenders, drugs.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.640
Well, breathe a
sigh of relief

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.720
because all we bring
you are the facts.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.160
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.720
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.400
Does even thinking about migraines
give you a headache?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.040
Well, you’re not alone.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.960
Migraines affect an estimated 10 percent
of the population worldwide.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:38.840
In our first story,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.320
we put plant based diets to the test
for treating migraine disorders.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.280
Headaches are one of the top five reasons
people end up in emergency rooms, and

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.320
one of the leading reasons for which
people see their doctors in general.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.640
One of the things you
can try to do prevent them

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.080
is to identify the triggers
and avoid them.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.080
Common triggers for migraines include
stress, smoke, hunger, sleep issues,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.800
certain trigger foods like
chocolate, cheese, and alcohol,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.000
your menstrual cycle, or
certain weather patterns.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.600
In terms of dietary treatments,
the Father of Modern Medicine,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.080
William Osler, suggested
trying a strict vegetable diet.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.240
After all, the nerve inflammation
associated with migraines may be

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.880
reduced by a strictly plant-based
diet, as many plant foods are high

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.120
in anti-inflammatory compounds
and antioxidants, and likewise,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.960
meat products may have
pro-inflammatory properties,

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:35.880
but it wasn't put to the test
for another 117 years.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.800
Among those given a
placebo supplement,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.280
half said they got better,
half said they didn't.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.200
But when put on a strictly plant-based
diet they did much better,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.280
experiencing a significant drop
in the severity of their pain.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.040
Now it's possible that the pain reducing
effects of the plant-based diet

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.640
may have at least been in part,
due to the weight reduction;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.880
they lost about 9 more pounds
in their vegan month.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.360
Even just lowering the fat
content of the diet may help.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.120
Those placed on a month of consuming
less than 30 grams of fat a day,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.000
like less than two tablespoons
of oil all day, experienced highly

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.840
significant decreases in headache
frequency, intensity, duration,

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:20.080
and the need to take medications, a six-
fold decrease in frequency and intensity.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.520
From three migraine attacks every
two weeks, down to just one a month.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.600
And by low fat they didn't
mean SnackWell's;

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.040
they meant more fruits,
vegetables, beans.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.960
Before the food industry co-opted
and corrupted the term,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:41.680
eating low fat meant like eating
an apple, not Apple Jacks.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.560
Now this was a really low-fat
diet, like 10% fat

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.920
for someone eating 2500 calories a day.
What about just less than 20% fat,

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.400
compared to a more normal, but still
relatively lower fat diet than average?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.120
Same significant drops in headache
frequency and severity,

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.840
including a 5-fold drop in
attacks of severe pain.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.880
Since the intervention involved at
least halving of saturated fat intake,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.760
mostly found in meat, dairy, and junk,
the researchers concluded

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.200
that a reduction of saturated fat
intake may help control migraine

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.240
attacks, but it's not necessarily
something that they're getting less of.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.680
There are compounds present
in live green real veggies

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:26.320
that might bind to a migraine-triggering
peptide known as CGRP.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.840
Drug companies have been trying to
come up with something that binds to it,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.160
but the drugs have failed to be
effective, and are also toxic,

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.720
a problem you don't see with cabbage.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.520
Green vegetables also have magnesium,
found throughout the food supply

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.000
but mostly concentrated
in green leafy vegetables,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.280
beans, nuts, seeds, and whole grains.
It's actually the central atom

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.840
to chlorophyll, so you can see
how much magnesium foods have

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.800
in the produce aisle by the
intensity of their green color.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.920
Magnesium supplements do not appear
to decrease migraine severity,

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.240
but may reduce the number of
attacks you get in the first place.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.280
You can ask your doctor about starting
600 mg of magnesium dicitrate every day,

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.760
but note, magnesium supplements can
cause adverse effects such as diarrhea,

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.200
so I recommend getting it
in the way nature intended.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.440
Any foods that may particularly help?
I've talked about ground ginger.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.580
Combining caffeine with over-the-counter
pain killers like Tylenol, aspirin and

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.560
ibuprofen may boost their
efficacy, about 130 milligrams

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.400
for tension-type headaches
and 100 mg for migraines,

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:40.560
about what you might expect to get
in three cups of tea, though I believe

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.400
it's just a coincidence that the
principle investigator was named Lipton.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.480
Note you can overdo it. If you take
kids and teens who have headaches,

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:53.440
drinking one and a half liters of
cola a day, and cut the cola,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.600
you can cure 90% of them, though
this may be a Coca-Cola effect

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.440
rather than a caffeine effect.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.440
Did you know that daily
application of capsaicin

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:09.800
results in up to an 80% therapeutic
response rate for a certain type of headache?

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.603
Here’s the story.

00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:14.000
It appeared worthwhile
to study the effects

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.200
produced by the topical
application of capsaicin

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.560
in the human nose.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.160
It therefore appeared
worthwhile because

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.200
it had never been
done before? OK...

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.000
So they took some
medical students

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.200
dripped some
in their nose

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.200
and they started sneezing,
burning, and snotting.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.640
Describing the pain as like 8 or 9
on a scale of 1 to 10.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.840
No surprise, but here's
the interesting part.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.720
What do you
think happened

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.360
when they repeated the
experiment the next day?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.960
You'd think they might
be sensitized to it,

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.840
still all irritated and so
it might hurt even worse,

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.680
but no, it hurt less.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.600
Then they did it again the next day

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.960
and the next.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.840
By day 5 it hardly
hurt at all,

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:02.120
they didn't even get a
runny nose, no sneezing.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:07.640
Came back the next week,
day ten and still nothing.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:11.680
Sheesh, were they like
permanently numbed?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.960
No, after a month or so the
desensitization wore off

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.960
and they were back
in agony whenever

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.520
they tried rubbing
it in their nose.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.560
What the researchers think
is happening is that

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.520
the pain fibers, the nerves
that carry pain sensation,

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.680
dumped so much of the
pain neurotransmitter

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.360
called substance P
that they ran out.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.400
Day after day of this the
nerves had exhausted

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.840
their stores and could no
longer transmit pain messages

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.520
until they made more
substance P from scratch,

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.560
which takes a
couple of weeks.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.480
This gave researchers an idea.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.160
There's a rare headache syndrome
called cluster headache.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.360
It has been described as one

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:54.840
of the worst pains
humans experience.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.400
Few, if any, medical disorders
are more painful.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.400
It's nicknamed the
"suicide headache"

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.400
because patients often
consider taking

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.640
or have taken their
lives over it.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.400
It's thought to be caused
by arterial dilation

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.520
putting pressure on the
trigeminal nerve in the face.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.520
Treatments involve everything

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.920
from nerve blocks to
botox to surgery.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:27.120
But hey, that same nerve
goes down to the nose.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.080
What if we cause
the whole nerve

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.520
to dump all its
substance P?

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:38.280
"Preventative effect of repeated nasal
applications of capsaicin in cluster headache".

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.280
Same as before,
capsaicin in the nose

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:44.360
and by day 5 they could
hardly feel it any more.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.120
Note though that these were
cluster headache sufferers

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.400
and so what was rated as an
8 or 9 on the pain scale

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.120
by the whimpy medical students
was like, maybe a 3 or 4

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.400
by those used to
the violence

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.320
of the cluster
headache attacks.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.040
Having achieved
desensitization,

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.320
what happened to
their headaches?

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.480
Well cluster headaches
are one-sided headaches,

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.560
you only get pain on
one side of your head.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.080
So those who had rubbed capsaicin
in the opposite nostril,

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.040
on the wrong side
of the head,

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.400
nothing happened.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.360
They started out having
like 40 attacks a day

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.080
and a month later the headaches
were still going strong,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.280
but those that rubbed the
capsaisin in the nostril

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.040
on the side of the head
where the headaches were,

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.280
cut the average number
of attacks in half.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.400
And in fact half the
patients were cured!

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.840
The cluster headaches
were gone completely.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.640
All in all 80%
responded,

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.840
at least equal
if not better

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:47.440
than all the current
therapies out there.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.160
Finally today,

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.440
we discover the power of
powdered ginger for migraines.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:56.120
Many successful herbal
treatments start like this.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.800
Some doctor learns that
some plant has been used

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.280
by some ancient medical tradition,
like ginger for headaches

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:04.960
and figures, hey, they've
got patients with headaches

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.520
and since its just
some safe common spice

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.520
advises one of their migraine
patients to give it a try.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.280
At the first sign of a migraine coming on,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.320
the patient mixed a quarter teaspoon
of powdered ginger in some water,

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.520
drank it down, and poof, within a half hour

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.400
the migraine went away.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.560
And it worked every time, no side-effects.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.560
This is what’s called a case report,

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:28.680
which is really
just a glorified anecdote,

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.080
but case reports have
played an important role

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.720
in the history of medicine.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.720
AIDS was first discovered
as a series of case reports.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.160
Some young guy walks
into a clinic in Los Angeles

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.200
with a bad case of thrush
and the rest is history.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.160
Or reports of an unusual side-effect
of a failed chest pain drug

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.200
leading to the billion
dollar blockbuster, Viagra.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:55.680
Case reports may be the ‘lowest’
or ‘weakest’ form of evidence,

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:58.680
but they are often the
‘first line of evidence.’

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.000
That’s where everything begins.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.000
So a report like this
isn’t helpful in and of itself,

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.400
but it can inspire researchers
to put it to the test.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.600
The problem is, who’s going to fund it?

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:16.160
The market for migraine drugs
is worth billions of dollars.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.800
A quarter teaspoon of powdered
ginger costs about a penny.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.240
So who’d fund a study pitting ginger

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.920
versus the leading migraine drug?

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.440
No one...

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.040
...until now.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.680
A double-blinded randomized
controlled clinical trial

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.920
comparing the efficacy
of ginger to sumatriptan,

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.040
also known as Imitrex,
one of the top-selling

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:38.120
billion dollar drugs in the world,

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.280
in the treatment of
migraine headaches.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.120
They tried using just
one eighth of a teaspoon

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.800
of powdered ginger versus
a good dose of the drug.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:52.240
And they both worked
just as well, just as fast.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.000
Most started out in moderate
or severe pain before,

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.440
but after the drug or ginger,

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.840
ended up mild or pain free.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.640
The same proportion of migraine
sufferers reported satisfaction

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.840
with the results either way,

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:07.960
and so as far as I’m
concerned ginger won,

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.480
not only because it’s a
few billion dollars cheaper

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.280
but because there were
significantly fewer

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.640
side-effects in the ginger group.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:18.560
On the drug people reported dizziness,
a sedative effect,

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:20.360
vertigo and heartburn.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.160
The only thing reported for
ginger was an upset tummy

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.240
in about 1 in of 25 people,

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.720
though taking a whole
tablespoon of ginger powder

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.120
at one time on an empty stomach

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.280
could irritate anyone’s tummy,
just as a note of caution.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.160
Sticking to an eighth of a teaspoon

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:38.880
is not only up to 3000 times
cheaper than the drug,

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:43.560
but you’re probably less likely to
end up as a case report yourself

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:52.360
of people that have had a heart attack
or died after taking the drug.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:54.640
